course: dictionary
lesson: 4047
title: Genes: the instructions you inherit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gene is a tiny part of the DNA inside the cells of a living thing. It carries instructions that are passed down from parents to children, such as the instructions for eye colour or the shape of a leaf.
explain: That is why you may look a bit like your mum or dad. You inherit genes from them. When people say «it's in the genes» or «it runs in the family», they mean that something is passed down through the family.
explain: Genes are not the only thing that matters. «Spots come mainly from hormones, skin and genes», so several things work together. «Curliness comes mostly from your genes», which is why eating crusts will not make your hair curly.
fact: A gene is a tiny part of DNA.
fact: DNA is found inside the cells of living things.
fact: Genes carry instructions that are passed from parents to children.
fact: «Studbooks» are family records that good zoos keep, so that rare animals are not too closely related.
fact: A healthy mix of genes helps animals survive disease and change.
exercise: What is a gene? | The name of a family dog | A type of cell that moves dust | *A tiny part of DNA that carries instructions | A huge bag of sweets
exercise: Why might a child have the same eye colour as a parent? | *Because they inherit genes from their parents | Because they eat the same food | Because they copy their parents' clothes | Because the sun makes them look alike
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Good zoos keep family records called studbooks» that names the family records. | zoos | animals | rare | *studbooks
test: «It's in the genes» is a phrase people use. What does it mean? | Someone is very tall | Something is written in a book | Someone has a cold | *Something is passed down through the family
test: «One gene decides whether earwax is dry and flaky or wet and sticky.» What does one gene decide? | The sound earwax makes | *Whether earwax is dry and flaky or wet and sticky | Where earwax is kept in the ear | How fast earwax grows
exam: Why is it true that «curliness comes mostly from your genes» and not from eating crusts? | Curly hair is caused by sunlight | Crusts make hair curly for a short time | Hair curls when it is cold | *Curliness comes from genes and the tiny pocket each hair grows from
